  "A_construction_method": "(a) boxed formula (S-matrix composition): A1 = S1 + S(f)^-1.S1.S2 + I, A2 = I + S2.S1.S(f).S1^-1 + S2.S1.S(f), built by composing the conjugation-action matrices S1, S2 (and S(f):=S_of_word(F), S(f)^-1:=S_of_word(inv(F)), each itself a product of S1/S2/S1inv/S2inv per the word's own letters) -- NOT via the finite-difference definition (b) (column j = Phi(R_i(f.n_j)) + Phi(R_i(f))), which was never used anywhere in this crosscheck's implementation.",
  "MAT_1_convention_declaration": {
